\title{llmCoder: Automated Mixed-Methods Coding with Large Language Models}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.svg}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Applies a qualitative codebook to text with large language models through 'ellmer' structured output, then links the resulting theme codes to participants' quantitative metadata. Validates the automated codes against a human-coded sample with Cohen's kappa, precision and recall, tests whether a numeric metric differs when each theme is present with Welch's t-test and multiple-comparison adjustment, and plots the results. Segment-level transcripts can be aggregated to participants before linking. Developed by Neudata Consulting Ltd.
